Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T22:44:57-07:00","id":901773,"title":"","content":"I meant more in regards to already existing contracts being listed as Affinity Contracts, but fair enough. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T07:33:41-07:00","id":902708,"title":"","content":"Court Contracts could be anything. We don't know if its based on Mantle, or if all Court Contracts will be a single Contract that will have all six Seemings for a bonus, or if there will be no Seemings and you just pick options per dot invested like Vainglory does.<br /> <br /> My guess is this:<ul><li> Courts will take the place of Seeming for affinities, and you'll work the Contracts the same way. So, for Contracts of Talespinning, you'll have a Ruby, Ivory, Silver, Brass and Jade option.</li> <li>All Courts will have Contracts of Emotion. You get your Court emotion as affinity, and can purchase other emotions for 1xp. You can even theoretically buy emotions not part of your Court system (ie a Silver Courtier of Toronto could buy Desire as an emotion, mimicking the old Spring Court, even though the Silver Court's emotion is Wrath).</li> <li>Court systems will have a Contract that's specific to that system. IE The Scheherazade has Talespinning, the Rose Courts would have the Contracts of Flowers, the Directional Courts would have Contracts of the Contracts of Four Directions.</li> <li>Each Court will have a single Contract unique to itself, unshared by any other Court.</li> <li>Mantle won't be rolled, but we'll keep the same X+Y+Wyrd roll.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T17:51:34-07:00","id":903874,"title":"","content":"All courts have access to Talespinning contracts. Speculation on my part, but Takespinning might be tied to your courts &quot;story&quot;.<br /> <br /> Contractcof Emotions isalso universal to all courts, but with a focus on the courts emotion.<br /> <br /> The Directional Courts appear to be unique as do the court conracts like Air and Darkness for the London Courts.<br /> <br /> On the other hand the Arts and Sciences Court appear to list preexisting contracts (Hidden Reality already exists and so I spuculate that there might a be a universal contract for perfection as yet unrevealed). What this mean for these contracts I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}